7] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186268390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268476 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2ab8e018-d349-5c74-b2e8-1930a7b5eded" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268529 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "49d228b2-8aea-57a5-b2ca-483e7c7b3e29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=e.$ Given that the point $P(e,2,3)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5c5dd738-1c94-548e-aa53-3b5d32dc4abc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268885 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=e.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(e,2,3)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(e,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(e,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(e,2) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(e,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(e,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =1(y-2) \\\\ z & =y+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(e,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=e \\\\ z=y+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321387 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y+8\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321387 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321387 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "204035e4-46d4-534d-ba05-15ce0e052f85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321868 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4x\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321868 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321868 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b70aad1-ccca-5779-affa-e5700fd0cc6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322059 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4y+8\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322059 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322059 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7510c1fa-11fc-530d-ac02-4cbbe0845097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322206 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4x+8\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322206 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322206 #edb/ref 1